  One thing I need to flag before detailed questions. The entire app right now is this:

  [90m<[34mh1[90m>[39mTasks[90m</[34mh1[90m>[39m
  [90m<[34mmain[90m></[34mmain[90m>[39m

  No tasks, no storage, no users, no server — and notifications presuppose all four. "Notify users when tasks they care
  about change" implies: a task model that persists, identity (who "a user" is), a way to express "care about," a
  change/event source, and a delivery channel. That's several subsystems, not one. So my first job is to find out what
  actually exists before designing against a blank page.

